.el .ds Aq '
.TH ifg-org 1  "ifg-org 0.8.1" 
.SH NAME
ifg\-org \- Work with organizations
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBifg org\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Work with organizations
.PP
Members are addressed by username: `org add\-member` resolves the name through `GET /users/{username}` and posts the numeric id, and `org members` shows the username the server resolves for each row (falling back to `#id` when the account is gone).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ifg\-org\-list(1)
List the organizations you belong to
.TP
ifg\-org\-view(1)
Show one organization
.TP
ifg\-org\-create(1)
Create an organization
.TP
ifg\-org\-members(1)
List an organization\*(Aqs members
.TP
ifg\-org\-add\-member(1)
Add a member by username
.TP
ifg\-org\-remove\-member(1)
Remove a member by username
.TP
ifg\-org\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH VERSION
v0.8.1
